\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang3081\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl256\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\faauto\sb0\sa160\hyphpar0\ltrpar\f7\fs22\lang3081\kerning1\cf0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl256\slmult1\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0\ltrpar\rtlch\af16 \ltrch\lang1033\hich\af8\loch\lang1033\f8\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang3081\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl256\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\faauto\sb0\sa160\hyphpar0\ltrpar\f7\fs22\lang3081\kerning1\cf0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl256\slmult1\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0\ltrpar{\rtlch\af16 \ltrch\lang1033\hich\af8\loch\lang1033\f8\loch
ZCC (Zachary C Compiler) is a C compiler designed to target ZaC-3, a 32-bit CPU. ZCC was originally designed for ZaC-1 which was 8-bit with 64KB of memory, but that was quickly very limited since C compiled programs used a lot of memory even for simple C programs. So then I designed a 16-bit CPU, and I had issues with segmented memory model so then I made a 32-bit CPU which inherits the RISC ISA design of the 16-bit but it\u8217\'92s just extended to 32-bits, and now that\u8217\'92s the new design. ZaC-3 has 4GB flat memory space as a result.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang3081\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl256\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\faauto\sb0\sa160\hyphpar0\ltrpar\f7\fs22\lang3081\kerning1\cf0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl256\slmult1\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0\ltrpar{\rtlch\af16 \ltrch\lang1033\hich\af8\loch\lang1033\f8\loch
The compiler has a lexer, AST and asm gen. There\u8217\'92s no IR so the asm gen looks at the AST and outputs ZaC-3 assembly directly. In the future when the compiler gets more advanced, I might make an IR to make feature implementation more simple.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang3081\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl256\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\faauto\sb0\sa160\hyphpar0\ltrpar\f7\fs22\lang3081\kerning1\cf0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl256\slmult1\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0\ltrpar{\rtlch\af16 \ltrch\lang1033\hich\af8\loch\lang1033\f8\loch
For expression parsing, the register file (there\u8217\'92s 32, 32-bit registers in ZaC-3) is used as the temporary result data stack. For the moment there\u8217\'92s no stack support for temporary results so it\u8217\'92s limited to 32 temporary results, which is actually still quite usable as long as individual expressions don\u8217\'92t get too long or complex.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang3081\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl256\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\faauto\sb0\sa160\hyphpar0\ltrpar\f7\fs22\lang3081\kerning1\cf0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl256\slmult1\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0\ltrpar{\rtlch\af16 \ltrch\lang1033\hich\af8\loch\lang1033\f8\loch
The stack is used for local variables and function parameters.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang3081\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl256\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\faauto\sb0\sa160\hyphpar0\ltrpar\f7\fs22\lang3081\kerning1\cf0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl256\slmult1\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0\ltrpar\rtlch\af16 \ltrch\lang1033\hich\af8\loch\lang1033\f8\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang3081\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl256\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\faauto\sb0\sa160\hyphpar0\ltrpar\f7\fs22\lang3081\kerning1\cf0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl256\slmult1\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0\ltrpar{\rtlch\af16 \ltrch\lang1033\hich\af8\loch\lang1033\f8\loch
